# A pref file supplied by a mod, in ui-prefs.c's own grammar.
#
# The point is that this is the SAME parser the game uses for a pref file the
# player loads by hand - there is not a second, mod-flavoured one. Anything
# legal in a user .prf is legal here, and anything illegal is reported on this
# mod's row in the manager rather than swallowed.
#
# One visible change, chosen to be obvious and harmless: open floor is drawn in
# white instead of dark grey, in every lighting variant, so a player enabling
# this mod can see at a glance that a mod's pref file was applied.
#
# feat:<code>:<lighting>:<attr>:<char>   attr 1 is COLOUR_WHITE, char 46 is '.'
feat:FLOOR:*:1:46
